    <h2 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.5rem;">SRO Register Index II Procedures & Revenue Land Classification Verification</h2>
    <p>In Indian property conveyancing and SRO administration, every physical or digital title registration generates an official entry in <strong>Register Index II</strong> maintained at the Sub-Registrar Office. Understanding how SRO index entries interact with revenue land classification records is crucial for preventing title disputes, invalid mortgages, and illegal layout acquisitions.</p>
    
    <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 25px;">Statutory Verification of Land Classifications & Zoning Compliance</h3>
    <ul style="padding-left: 20px;">
        <li><strong>Agricultural Land Conversion (CLU / N.A. Order):</strong> Verify that non-agricultural residential or commercial construction is backed by an official Change of Land Use (CLU) order issued by the District Collector or Revenue Divisional Officer (RDO).</li>
        <li><strong>Prohibited Properties List (Section 22A Clearance):</strong> Ensure the property survey number is not listed under Section 22A of the Registration Act. Section 22A includes government lands, ceiling surplus lands, temple endowment lands, and assigned lands prohibited from private transfer.</li>
        <li><strong>Town Planning Approval (DTCP / HMDA / BDA / CMDA):</strong> Confirm that layout plot developments are formally approved by regional urban development authorities with assigned LP numbers.</li>
        <li><strong>Gram Panchayat vs Urban Local Body Jurisdiction:</strong> Verify whether the property falls under Gram Panchayat yellow zone boundaries or municipal corporation expansion limits for property tax assessment.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 25px;">Step-by-Step Guidance for Resolving SRO Record Discrepancies</h3>
    <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
        <li><strong>Survey Number Mismatches:</strong> If survey numbers differ between SRO title deeds and revenue Patta/RTC records, obtain an official Survey Correlation Certificate from the Tahsildar office.</li>
        <li><strong>Missing SRO Index Entries:</strong> If a registered sale deed fails to appear on online EC portals, submit a certified physical copy of the registered deed to the SRO for manual index entry update.</li>
        <li><strong>Unreleased Bank Mortgages:</strong> If a historic bank loan entry appears without a cancellation receipt, approach the lending bank with full loan closure receipts to execute a registered Release Deed.</li>
    </ol>
